  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Branch (constraint 1); declare FULL rigor; rebase on master; /conflict-check for RecordCreationService.cs (041 and UAC-r2).</step>
    <step order="1">Invert A1-A3 and write the must-fire tests of §15.6 and AC4-AC9 failing first.</step>
    <step order="2">Split StampBeforeCreateAsync; step 6½ plans; step 7 asks over lookups ∪ derived; step 10 binds and sets I-16 with no second derivation.</step>
    <step order="3">Repair: plan once before RepairOwnerAsync, add to keyed, hand the result to RepairStampAsync; planning fault keeps the owner (AC8).</step>
    <step order="4">Run the parity theory; fix or file each difference it finds (AC9, AC10).</step>
    <step order="5">Reconcile §15.5's step-8 bullet with 041 (AC13). Build; filtered suites and ArchTests; publish delta; CVE.</step>
    <step order="6">Two adversarial passes (security tag); then send the diff to UAC-r2 for the full pass (AC15). Fix every finding. Record in notes/task-042b-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="7">After merge: close DI-009 and #2483 with the PR link; update TASK-INDEX to `✅ [done]`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the parity theory shows a difference that can be closed only by changing the reconciler or RecordOwnershipResolver outside OwnerQuestionOf / ForRow, STOP: file it as its own issue with a DI entry (per /project-defer-issue-tracking) and escalate before widening scope.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any single-condition refusal code, status or word would change, or a new AppendTo probe would be needed, STOP and escalate to UAC-r2 (NFR-07, ADR-008 path A).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the reconciler does NOT refuse row 7 (report-card child whose root's BU has no default team) the way the create does, fix it here only if the fix stays inside OwnerQuestionOf / ForRow; otherwise STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

