  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1: the create order is design §15.3: 6½ plans the missing stamp (same codes, words and trace step StampAndInheritance: 400 stamp_underivable, 503 stamp_unavailable) for every principal; step 7 asks over LookupsOf(item) ∪ {derived column → RecordOwnershipParent(root)} through OwnerQuestionOf / ForRow; step 10 binds and sets I-16 from the 6½ result with no second PlanMissingStampAsync call (asserted by call count); the bind refusals (500 no_decision, 503) stay at step 10; the system principal still binds after the create (DI-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2: A1-A3 are inverted: A1 and A3 are owned by SecureNamedTeam with the sharee mirror written at create; A2 agrees with the create; a chat twin in ChatCreatedChildStampTests passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3 (change 1): a to-do with no pair under a team-owned report card in BU X, whose matter is in BU Y, is owned by Y's team; the same with the to-do's pair set is owned by X.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4 (UAC-r2 condition (a), row 5): two tests, one for the transient Make Secure interval (sprk_issecure set, Secure team not yet assigned) and one for the lasting compensated state, each refuse 409 SecureParentNotIsolated and create nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5 (UAC-r2 condition (b)): the row-5 refusal's code, status and detail text equal the existing direct-child C11 refusal's ("re-run Make Secure on it, then retry"), asserted verbatim; grep finds no SecuringRoot (or equivalent) exemption in src.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6 (row 2 order): a root read fault combined with an owner world that refuses gives 503 stamp_unavailable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7 (creator visibility, UAC-r2): a caller who is not a sharee of the Secure matter gets the normal 201 for the A1 create; the response body contains no secure-family id (matter, team or BU) beyond the ids the caller sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8 (Repair, UAC-r2 condition (c)): a user-owned to-do missing its stamp under a team-owned invoice of a Secure matter is re-owned to Secure and stamped in one update. If planning faults, the owner is kept (never re-owned over the lookups alone), the repair result reports the owner part Skipped with record_repair.stamp_unavailable, and a log line carries the row id and the reason; a test asserts the report entry and the log.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC9 (parity theory): for every RecordTableRules table with IsStampedChildEntity (to-do, event, memo, analysis, communication, Signal, Decision Record), in a secure world and an ordinary world, the create's owner equals ResolveOwnerAsync(ForExistingRowAsync(written row)). The theory includes a communication carrying sprk_communicationthread.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC10 (thread filing, UAC-r2 Q3): if AC9 shows a create can carry sprk_communicationthread and the owners differ, the record-thread filing is added inside OwnerQuestionOf / ForRow the way RecordCreationService.cs ~:1183-1187 handles Repair, and AC9 passes; only if it needs a different seam is it filed as its own issue with a DI entry in notes/defer-issues.md, and the theory case is marked with that issue.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC11 (row 7 parity, UAC-r2): the parity test shows the reconciler refuses the report-card child whose root's BU has no default team the same way the create does (409); a disagreement is fixed here.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC12 (negative): ChatCreatedChildStampTests ~:106 stays green and its comment at ~:108-110 is rewritten; step 5's AppendTo probes are identical (no new probe; the derived root is never asked as the caller); EmailDraftRecordCreationTests' owner and AppendTo calls are unchanged; a browser-sent stamp derives nothing and leaves the question unchanged; a document (seam ~:229) and a work assignment (seam ~:64) derive nothing; RouteCreatePreCreateStampTests ~:64, ~:81, seam ~:84-148, ChildRecordCreateRefusalContractTests, CrossSurfaceOwnerTests ~:78-144, OfficeRecordOwnershipTests and SecureRootCreateRouteTests.Office* pass with unchanged assertions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC13 (§15.5 with 041): if 041 merged first, there is no step-8 index assertion (step 8 is NoOp) and §15.5's step-8 bullet in design.md is updated to say so; if 041 has not merged, the A1/A3 must-fire asserts "the event's index is empty and search_index_unset_for_owner_bu is logged" and the notes record that 041 updates it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC14: the PR records design §15.4 rows 1-7 as K lines (rows 2 and 5 covered by AC6 and AC4); BFF build 0 errors; filtered suites (SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, RecordCreationServicePipelineSeamTests*, ChatCreatedChildStampTests, WriterBuilderOwnershipParityTests, RecordRepairModeTests, EmailDraftRecordCreationTests, CrossSurfaceOwnerTests, ChildRecordCreateRefusalContractTests, Office* ownership suites) and ArchTests pass; publish-size delta against a fresh master build (both sizes, file counts, zip tool) and the CVE result are recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC15 (UAC-r2): UAC-r2 receives the diff before merge and does a full pass; its verdict line is in the PR and every finding is fixed or filed. DI-009 and #2483 close on merge with the PR link.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract (AC1-AC13) and the §15.6 must-fire and must-not-fire lists. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes. One seeding proof: break the step-7 inclusion of the derived root once and show A1 fails (recorded, reverted).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Placement Justification (CLAUDE.md §10, bff-extensions.md): a modification inside RecordCreationService (and .Repair.cs) in the BFF, where the synchronous write path that owns I-1 and I-6 lives; no new endpoint, service, package or background work; expected publish delta ≈ 0, measured against a fresh master build (§10 bullet 4); CVE check run.
§11: no new surface. Two private halves of an existing method and one extra argument to a private method are a pure modification (design §15.7).
ADR-008 path A: step 5 unchanged; derivation app-only behind the caller's AppendTo on the intermediate. ADR-002: create and reconciler ask one question, built by ForRow.
Release note: during Make Secure, a create under a root flagged secure but not yet isolated now refuses 409 (UAC-r2 accepted).
Added 2026-11-02 by the scope path (design §15 → UAC-r2 review → spec FR-41 → this task → TASK-INDEX → owner approval). Awaiting owner approval.</notes>

